 or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"A new Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) has been submitted for review. Please analyze the following DEP and respond with only \\\"APPROVE\\\" if you approve it, or \\\"DENY\\\" followed by your reasoning if you deny it.\\n\\n---BEGIN USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\nQuestion: Hello! I’m Delta, your Chief of Staff. How can I help you today?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Great! To tailor the website to your vision, could you share any visual style or design inspirations you have in mind (colors, logos, or websites you like)?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Do you already own a domain name or hosting plan, or would you like help setting that up?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Who will be responsible for adding and updating content such as News & Events, and how comfortable are they with technology?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: How should new residents obtain login access—should they be able to self-register, or will an administrator add them manually?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Should the News & Events section be viewable by anyone, or reserved only for logged-in residents?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Do you have a preferred budget range or constraints for hosting and ongoing maintenance?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Do you already have email hosting for dunbaroakshoa.com, or would you like us to set up email forwarding/hosted mailboxes (for example, Google Workspace) as part of this project?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Which company currently manages your domain registration for dunbaroakshoa.com (e.g., GoDaddy, Namecheap, etc.)? This helps us give you precise DNS instructions.\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: For the Dues page, do you need residents to pay online on the site now, or is it enough to provide a downloadable dues schedule or an external payment link?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: On the Contact Us page, would you prefer a simple email link or a full site-based contact form with spam protection (reCAPTCHA)?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Do you need the website to support any languages besides English?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Do you already have a logo or other branding assets you’d like us to use, or should we proceed with a simple text-based placeholder logo until one is provided?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: What email address would you like us to place on the Contact Us page (e.g., your personal or board address)?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Do you have a Google account you’re happy to use for automated backups (UpdraftPlus → Google Drive)? If so, please share the Gmail address; if not, we can store backups only on the hosting platform.\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Will you purchase the SiteGround StartUp plan yourself (approx. $48 for the first promo year) or would you prefer we handle the signup once you provide payment details?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: Can you provide access to your Squarespace domain dashboard (or be available to add the A and CNAME records when we reach that step)?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\n---END USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\n\\n---BEGIN DEP---\\n**COMBINED FINAL DEP – Dunbar Oaks HOA Website**\\nPrepared for Execution Phase\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nPART A – TECHNICAL BUILD & DEPLOYMENT  (from impl-plan-final-v1)\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n1  Hosting\\n   • Use SiteGround “StartUp” Managed-WP plan – promo $3.99/mo → $17.99/mo renewal.\\n\\n2  Domain / DNS  (Registrar: Squarespace)\\n   • After SiteGround account creation note <SITEGROUND_SERVER_IP>.\\n   • Squarespace → Domains → dunbaroakshoa.com → DNS SETTINGS → Custom Records:\\n       – A   @    → <SITEGROUND_SERVER_IP>\\n       – CNAME www → @\\n   • Save, wait ≈1 h propagation (verify with dig).\\n   • Rollback: delete the two records to return traffic to Squarespace default site.\\n\\n3  WordPress Installation @ SiteGround\\n   • Site Tools → WordPress → Install latest-stable (record exact version).\\n   • Issue Let’s Encrypt SSL; Site Tools → Security → HTTPS Enforce = ON.\\n   • Rollback: SG one-click restore to pre-install backup.\\n\\n4  Plugin Stack (all free tiers)\\n   | Function                               | Plugin                    |\\n   |----------------------------------------|---------------------------|\\n   | Resident self-register + admin approval| WP User Manager 2.8.x     |\\n   | Page restriction                       | Restrict User Access 2.4.x|\\n   | Firewall / 2FA optional                | Wordfence 7.11.x          |\\n   | Back-ups → Google Drive (opt-in)       | UpdraftPlus 1.23.x        |\\n   | Caching                                | SG Optimizer 7.x (bundled)|\\n   Config details:\\n   • WPUM → Registration ON, Admin Approval.\\n   • RUA → Create level “Residents”; restrict Dues & Annual Meetings pages.\\n   • Wordfence → WAF extended; 2FA optional.\\n   • UpdraftPlus → connect Gmail ethanm938@gmail.com; daily files+DB; retain 30 copies.\\n   • SG Optimizer → Dynamic caching, GZIP, browser caching.\\n   Rollback: deactivate individual plugin or SG restore point.\\n\\n5  Page Creation & Protection\\n   • Create pages: Home, News & Events, Bylaws, Schools, Contact Us, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings (protected).\\n   • Restrict Dues & Annual Meetings to Residents role.\\n\\n6  Contact Page\\n   • Paragraph with mail link: ethanm938@gmail.com (mailto).\\n\\n7  Backups & Recovery\\n   • SiteGround nightly automated backups ×30 days.\\n   • UpdraftPlus daily off-site (if configured).  Quarterly restore test to staging sub-domain.\\n   • Recovery: SG restore UI → choose date; verify site integrity.\\n\\n8  Execution-Phase Checklist\\n   E-1  User purchases SG plan & provides credentials.\\n   E-2  Add primary domain; obtain server IP.\\n   E-3  User adds A & CNAME at Squarespace; verify propagation.\\n   E-4  Issue SSL; enforce HTTPS.\\n   E-5  Install WordPress.\\n   E-6  Remove default content/plugins.\\n   E-7  Install & configure plugins (§4).\\n   E-8  Create pages & restrict access (§5).\\n   E-9  Build menu; set Home static page.\\n   E-10 Enable SG Optimizer caching; test with GTMetrix (<2 s load).\\n   E-11 Connect UpdraftPlus to Gmail; run first manual backup.\\n   E-12 Wordfence initial scan; address findings.\\n   E-13 Create test Resident user; verify registration & restrictions.\\n   E-14 Generate admin HOW-TO PDF; store in CFS.\\n   E-15 Final QA; handover.\\n\\n   Contingency: any blocking failure → revert via latest SG backup and investigate root cause.\\n\\nExternal variables captured during execution:\\n   • SiteGround credentials & payment (user-provided)\\n   • Squarespace login (user action for DNS)\\n   • Actual server IP after provisioning\\n   • Gmail OAuth token (if UpdraftPlus enabled)\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nPART B – VISUAL DESIGN & CONTENT STRATEGY  (from design-plan-final-v1)\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\n1  Style Guide\\n   • Colors: #1E6EB4 primary, #F4B400 secondary, #222 text, #FFFFFF bg, #F7F9FC muted bg, #D6DEE6 border.\\n   • Typography: Headings – Poppins 600/500; Body – Roboto 400, 18 px / 1.6.\\n   • Placeholder logo: Site Title text (primary color, 24 px, weight 700).\\n\\n2  Theme – Astra (free)\\n   • Appearance → Themes → Add New → Astra → Install & Activate.\\n   • Customize:\\n     – Global Typography & Colors per guide.\\n     – Header Builder: Site Title left, Primary Menu center.\\n     – Footer: two-row; © current-year HOA.\\n     – Layout: Container width 1240 px boxed.\\n   • Rollback: switch to default Twenty Twenty-Four; remove customizer settings via Astra reset.\\n\\n3  Navigation Structure\\n   Home | News & Events | Bylaws | Schools | Contact Us | M